libtiffanydb (1.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Public API surface: sql_hist_jev is now declared in banco/sql_api.h. It
    was already exported (added in c6ff1c4); it had simply never been
    declared in an installed header.
  * Declaring it adds no exported symbol. It restores the invariant: declared
    and not exported = 0, exported and not declared = 0.
  * Structural surface is now 46 symbols = 43 functions (33 sql_*, 6 jev_*,
    4 pgwire_*) + 3 extern long. This is a count derived from the sources,
    not an nm -D measurement; the only nm -D measurement on record remains
    the V1 build (T=36, D/B=3, 39 symbols in total).
  * This is an update on top of the 45-symbol state recorded in 1.1.0-1. The
    1.1.0-1 entry below is left as written.
  * debian/control: the installed public headers are sql_api.h, pgwire_api.h
    and jev_api.h. jev_api.h was already being installed by debian/rules and
    listed in libtiffanydb-dev.install, so the omission was a documentation
    error and not a packaging one.
  * SONAME, install rules and the two-package split are unchanged.

 -- Tiffany DB Maintainers <tiffanydb@example.invalid>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

libtiffanydb (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * First Debian/Ubuntu packaging of the Tiffany DB shared library.
  * JEV integration: banco/jev.c, banco/jev_api.h, banco/jev_core.h,
    tests/jev_casos.c, tests/jev_casos.h, tests/test_jev_api.c,
    tests/test_jev_oraculo.c, JEV.md. 6 new public symbols:
    jev_arena, jev_marginal, jev_escore, jev_duas, jev_marginal_d, jev_proj.
    SONAME libtiffanydb.so.1 preserved. ABI: 39 + 6 = 45.
  * Two binary packages: libtiffanydb1 (runtime) and libtiffanydb-dev
    (headers, static library, pkg-config). Both are Multi-Arch: same.
  * SONAME is libtiffanydb.so.1. Packaging did not bump the ABI and did not
    change the product version: 1.0.0 is the product, -1 is the Debian
    revision.
  * No tiffany-db package: the command line frontend does not exist yet and
    this packaging does not invent one.
  * Packaged from the committed sources only. The product sources are not
    modified by this package.

 -- Tiffany DB Maintainers <tiffanydb@example.invalid>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000